      "label": "Validate direction, then reverse",
      "predicate": "TXN-TYPE = REV after TXN-DR-CR validated as D or C",
      "uncertainties": [
        "A rejected reversal can leave its input direction swapped; replaying the same record can toggle it again.",
        "No original transaction lookup or original journal validation is implemented."
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:rose:rule.txn_gl_routing",
      "@type": "rose:BusinessRule",
      "description": "Deposit subtype CH/SV/MM/CD maps to GL 4010/4030/4040/4050, otherwise 9999. DEP emits debit 1010 / credit deposit-GL; WDL debit deposit-GL / credit 1010; FEE debit deposit-GL / credit 7500; INT debit 8010 / credit deposit-GL. REV uses swapped direction for cash/deposit mapping. Other types emit 9999/9999. Amount is copied and post flag is Y.",
      "epistemic_status": "observed",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "end_line": 310,
          "excerpt_sha256": "f33e6da56e29e5d0536816644879a43a4503752bed89a33f94fb5f0088ee8508",
          "path": "src/TXNPOST0.cob",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/NSEvent/cobol-banking-system/blob/03ea874c84b5c00b11b78c6ca1498ec1a9cb7bb4/src/TXNPOST0.cob#L260-L310",
          "start_line": 260
        }
      ],
      "label": "Map a GL instruction",
      "uncertainties": [
        "Transaction type and debit/credit direction are independent inputs; DEP with D is not rejected, so account arithmetic and GL intent can disagree.",
        "REV uses cash/deposit routing and does not reconstruct arbitrary original fee/interest journals.",
        "A suspense mapping still returns post flag Y; no manual-review workflow is implemented."
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:rose:rule.txn_local_ctr_flag",
      "@type": "rose:BusinessRule",
      "description": "CHECK-CTR sets TXN-CTR-REPORTABLE=Y only when TXN-CASH-AMOUNT > 10000.00; equality yields N. This local check does not call BSACTRO or examine exemption/customer totals.",
      "effect": "Set Y, otherwise N. Source constant is US-oriented and not an Italian regulatory rule.",
      "epistemic_status": "observed",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "end_line": 320,
          "excerpt_sha256": "c67361f6e18f5f9c7f01fd24d04e03dd24a99aa7807e9b58a4d6a1d2d2732594",
